# DAY 28
R.append(("""That opening move is small and it does a great deal. A family that hears their own words from ten months ago read back to them understands immediately that this is a continuing thing rather than an event, and that understanding does more for their commitment than any amount of encouragement from you.""",
"""That opening move is small and it does a great deal. A family that hears their own words from ten months ago read back to them understands immediately that this is a continuing thing rather than an event, and that understanding does more for their commitment than any amount of encouragement from you.

It also does not have to be perfect, and I would say that to any family that is hesitating. It just needs to be intentional. The families who sustain this are not running impressive meetings. They are running ordinary ones, on purpose, on a schedule, and letting the accumulation do the work.

Eventually something changes that you cannot engineer. It stops being an event the family submits to and becomes simply how this family operates. Normal rather than unusual or difficult. That is the point at which your work is finished, and it is also the point at which nobody thanks you for it."""))

# DAY 29
R.append(("""So the question I would have you ask about your quietest client families is not whether they are getting on. It is when was the last time anything was actually put to them.""",
"""So the question I would have you ask about your quietest client families is not whether they are getting on. It is when was the last time anything was actually put to them.

There is a way to test it that does not manufacture a conflict. You put something real in front of them while the stakes are low and you watch. Not a decision. A question with a genuine edge on it, the kind a person could reasonably disagree with, asked in a room where disagreeing costs nothing yet.

A family in genuine alignment will answer it and move on. A family holding an avoidance will do something you can see. The room will go flat, or one person will answer for everybody, or somebody will change the subject skillfully. You will know within ninety seconds which one you have, and you will have found out in a year where finding out is cheap."""))

